    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WvunRxqLgBGFzjJ85aXPfJ)_\n\n## What\n\nSia asked to leave service mode with the same keys that enter it (Caps+Shift+;) instead of Esc.\n\n- `aerospace-keys.lua`: Caps+Shift+; now asks AeroSpace for the current mode (`aerospace list-modes --current`) and switches to `main` if it is `service`, otherwise to `service`. If that command fails (an old AeroSpace), it only enters the service mode, as before.\n- `aerospace.org`: key list updated. Esc and Caps+Esc from #312 stay as other ways out.\n\n## Not run, and what to check\n\nNo Mac or AeroSpace here, and I have not confirmed `list-modes --current` exists in your AeroSpace version (it should in recent releases). After `git pull` and a Hammerspoon reload: Caps+Shift+; enters, Caps+Shift+; again leaves. If it only ever enters, run `aerospace list-modes --current` in Terminal and send me the output.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAZg8pR9NBT6MCe97U)_",
